Subject: [PATCH] tb710fu: do not arm a kernel panic for watchdogd's backend-less exit

pl45b (run 45563220726) reached a full WindowServer + loginwindow userspace
and then panicked at pid 262:

  panic(cpu 2 caller 0xfffffff00c30407c): watchdogd[262] exited -- exit reason
  namespace 2 subcode 0x5 description: none

namespace 2 is OS_REASON_SIGNAL and subcode 0x5 is SIGTRAP, i.e. watchdogd did
not exit normally: it trapped. The reason is the board's hardware, not the
daemon:

  * this port has no AppleARMWatchdogTimer/AppleARMWatchdog backend matched by
    the profile, so IOWatchDogTimer lookup fails;
  * watchdogd's own failure paths differ by kern.hv_vmm_present
    (.work/UniXNU/scripts/check-watchdogd-branches.py emulates both):
      physical_missing (service=0, vmm=0) -> brk #1 at 0x10000ab0c  [SIGTRAP]
      virtual_missing  (service=0, vmm=1) -> exit(0)
    TB710FU is not a VMM guest from watchdogd's point of view, so it takes the
    brk #1 arm on every launch;
  * launchd spawns com.apple.watchdogd as a critical job
    (POSIX_SPAWN_PANIC_ON_CRASH), so proc_should_trigger_panic() returns true
    and proc_handle_critical_exit() panics the kernel.

package/BootWatchdogPolicy.c already writes launchd's
/private/var/db/com.apple.xpc.launchd/disabled.plist override (plus the empty
.migrated marker) for disable-watchdogd=1, and it reported status=0 on that
boot. That override only gates job import, and the job still ran: COM5 shows
"exec: pid 84 watchdogd" in launchd's startup wave and later
"exec: pid 239 xpcproxy" -> "exec: pid 239 watchdogd". A launchd-side override
therefore cannot be the only line of defence for a daemon whose hardware
backend does not exist.

This patch makes the kernel honour the board's own statement instead:
disable-watchdogd=1 means "no watchdog backend", so a watchdogd critical exit
is reported and suppressed rather than turned into a kernel panic. launchd
(initproc) keeps its always-panic rule, panic_on_crash_disabled keeps working,
and every other critical job keeps the upstream behaviour; a boot without
disable-watchdogd=1 is unchanged.

Once the panic no longer fires, panic_spin_forever() is reached and patch 0049's
tb710fu_cdc_panic_drain()/tb710fu_cdc_panic_loop() hand-over runs, so the next
failure still delivers its log over COM5 instead of resetting the SoC.

Source: pristine XNU ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f with patches
0001..0049 applied in series order; kern_exit.c is otherwise touched by 0002
(exit trace), 0004 (exec-log) and the boot-progress hunks only.

Reason: a daemon that cannot work on this board must not be able to panic the
kernel; the boot argument that documents the missing backend is the correct,
narrow switch.

Verification: git apply -v --check on the applied series fixture
(.work/xnu-patch-lf-clean, XNU ac9718f). The address evidence for the pl45b
panic path is in patch 0049's header (SavePanicInfo data abort at NULL + 0xc).
Hardware behaviour (watchdogd no longer panics the boot, WindowServer keeps the
GOP display) still requires a native run.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
index b5633e4..3e1f4a2 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@
 #include <sys/proc_info.h>
 #include <sys/reason.h>
 #include <sys/_types/_timeval64.h>
+#include <pexpert/pexpert.h> /* PE_parse_boot_argn() for disable-watchdogd */
 #include <sys/user.h>
 #include <sys/aio_kern.h>
 #include <sys/sysproto.h>
@@ -1838,6 +1839,49 @@ _proc_is_fatal_reason(os_reason_t reason)
 
 static TUNABLE(bool, panic_on_crash_disabled, "panic_on_crash_disabled", false);
 
+#if defined(XNU_TB710FU_MACOS27_SERVICES) && XNU_TB710FU_MACOS27_SERVICES
+/*
+ * TB710FU has no AppleARMWatchdogTimer backend behind IOWatchDogTimer.
+ * com.apple.watchdogd probes that service on start; when the lookup fails on a
+ * bare-metal boot (kern.hv_vmm_present == 0) it deliberately executes brk #1
+ * and is reaped as OS_REASON_SIGNAL / SIGTRAP (exit reason namespace 2 subcode
+ * 0x5 - see .work/UniXNU/scripts/check-watchdogd-branches.py, which shows the
+ * physical_missing arm trapping while the virtual_missing arm only exits 0).
+ * launchd spawns the job critical (POSIX_SPAWN_PANIC_ON_CRASH), so every
+ * watchdogd exit lands here and panics the kernel: pl45b (run 45563220726)
+ * panicked at watchdogd[262] right after WindowServer came up.
+ *
+ * package/BootWatchdogPolicy.c already writes launchd's disabled.plist override
+ * for disable-watchdogd=1, but that override only gates plist import and the job
+ * still ran (COM5: exec pid 84 watchdogd, then xpcproxy -> pid 239 watchdogd).
+ * The boot argument is this board's statement that no watchdog backend exists,
+ * so its daemon's crash must not be armed as a kernel panic. launchd itself and
+ * every other critical job keep the upstream behaviour.
+ */
+static bool
+tb710fu_watchdogd_exit_is_suppressed(proc_t p, int rv)
+{
+	static int disable_watchdogd = -1;
+
+	if (disable_watchdogd < 0) {
+		unsigned int enabled = 0;
+
+		disable_watchdogd =
+		    (PE_parse_boot_argn("disable-watchdogd", &enabled, sizeof(enabled)) &&
+		    (enabled == 1u)) ? 1 : 0;
+	}
+	if (disable_watchdogd != 1) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	if (strncmp(p->p_name, "watchdogd", sizeof("watchdogd") - 1) != 0 ||
+	    p->p_name[sizeof("watchdogd") - 1] != '\0') {
+		return false;
+	}
+	printf("TB710FU boot-policy: watchdogd critical exit suppressed (rv=0x%x)\n", rv);
+	return true;
+}
+#endif /* XNU_TB710FU_MACOS27_SERVICES */
+
 static bool
 proc_should_trigger_panic(proc_t p, int rv)
 {
@@ -1846,6 +1896,12 @@ proc_should_trigger_panic(proc_t p, int rv)
 		return true;
 	}
 
+#if defined(XNU_TB710FU_MACOS27_SERVICES) && XNU_TB710FU_MACOS27_SERVICES
+	if (tb710fu_watchdogd_exit_is_suppressed(p, rv)) {
+		return false;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	if (panic_on_crash_disabled) {
 		printf("panic-on-crash disabled via boot-arg\n");
 		return false;
